WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.324 --> 00:00:03.721
- I think people say I
look a bit like a queen

00:00:03.721 --> 00:00:05.471
in this outfit, yeah.

00:00:06.436 --> 00:00:09.698
And people call me Your Majesty.

00:00:09.698 --> 00:00:11.671
People come up and they curtsy.

00:00:11.671 --> 00:00:14.353
It's almost like living two lives, really.

00:00:14.353 --> 00:00:16.037
Let's commence.

00:00:16.037 --> 00:00:18.537
(royal music)

00:00:23.519 --> 00:00:27.971
I'm Ella Slack, and I'm
the Queen's stand-in.

00:00:27.971 --> 00:00:31.523
I've done it for over 30 years now.

00:00:31.523 --> 00:00:35.475
Anything that the Queen does is rehearsed.

00:00:35.475 --> 00:00:37.413
If it's just going to a town hall

00:00:37.413 --> 00:00:41.054
or opening a hospital, I've probably been

00:00:41.054 --> 00:00:45.314
a stand-in Queen, definitely
more than 50 times.

00:00:45.314 --> 00:00:47.155
A stand-in is not a look-alike.

00:00:47.155 --> 00:00:48.965
I don't look like the Queen.

00:00:48.965 --> 00:00:52.832
But I'm the same sort
of stature and height.

00:00:52.832 --> 00:00:55.517
I'm about, virtually five foot.

00:00:55.517 --> 00:00:57.268
The Queen's about five foot two.

00:00:57.268 --> 00:01:00.768
I live at Royal Court on Queens Promenade,

00:01:02.946 --> 00:01:05.655
in Royal Ramsey in the Isle of Man.

00:01:05.655 --> 00:01:09.822
And the Queen lives in
Buckingham Palace, in London.

00:01:11.895 --> 00:01:14.728
I drive a Ford gear automatic car.

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:19.563
The Queen has been seen
to drive Range Rovers

00:01:19.563 --> 00:01:23.525
and most of the time, she's
in a chauffeur-driven car

00:01:23.525 --> 00:01:24.942
or in a carriage.

00:01:27.215 --> 00:01:29.635
Well, it started because I was at the BBC

00:01:29.635 --> 00:01:32.535
and the producer who
was doing The Cenotaph

00:01:32.535 --> 00:01:35.175
came to see me and said that the Queen

00:01:35.175 --> 00:01:38.515
had sent a message to say,
when she stood at the Cenotaph,

00:01:38.515 --> 00:01:40.845
the sun was in her eyes,

00:01:40.845 --> 00:01:42.805
and so could we do anything about it?

00:01:42.805 --> 00:01:44.445
Well, I said to him, would you like me

00:01:44.445 --> 00:01:47.085
to come and stand in the position for you,

00:01:47.085 --> 00:01:50.095
because all the stage
managers were six foot men.

00:01:50.095 --> 00:01:51.845
And then that led on to other things.

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:53.655
I went in her royal carriage

00:01:53.655 --> 00:01:57.545
and rode on the boat up
to the Tower of London.

00:01:57.545 --> 00:02:00.725
And then there will be the
state opening of Parliament.

00:02:00.725 --> 00:02:04.015
I've never been allowed
to sit on the throne

00:02:04.015 --> 00:02:05.775
in the House of Lords.

00:02:05.775 --> 00:02:07.505
I have to lurk above it.

00:02:07.505 --> 00:02:09.625
It's a very strict rule.

00:02:09.625 --> 00:02:12.662
If I'm in a carriage
or a car, I will wave.

00:02:12.662 --> 00:02:15.495
You know, do like that, like that.

00:02:17.584 --> 00:02:19.651
The events that I've been helping with

00:02:19.651 --> 00:02:22.556
are events that are transmitted worldwide,

00:02:22.556 --> 00:02:25.159
and millions of people are going to watch.

00:02:25.159 --> 00:02:28.910
I look afterwards, and watch
the programs going out,

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:30.604
and I'll see her there,

00:02:30.604 --> 00:02:32.937
and think, I did it for you.

